{"Same-key builds race: Concurrent searches can both see a cache miss for the same NamespacedResource and enter BuildIndex before either stores b.cache[key]. File-backed indexes then race on the same Bleve directory, while memory-backed indexes duplicate the full storage scan and publish whichever build finishes last.": 0.9569146037101746, "Watcher starts after snapshot: When another writer commits a resource after search.init has read its startup snapshot but before initWatcher subscribes, the server misses both the indexed document and the watch event. The object can stay missing or stale in search until a later rebuild.": 0.936873197555542}